          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: નસ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "નસ — nas — \"a vein; a nerve\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "દાક્તરે મારા હાથની નસ તપાસી. dāktare mārā hāthnī nas tapāsī. The doctor examined the vein in my arm."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "નસ (nas) is inherited from Sanskrit snasā, \"tendon, muscle\"; CDIAL lists the Gujarati word, \"vein, nerve, tendon\" (CDIAL 13784)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
